<title>UK: Lufthansa Cargo orders up to 12 MD-11s.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa Cargo orders up to 12 MD-11s.</headline>
<dateline>FARNBOROUGH, England 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lufthansa Cargo AG said it has ordered five McDonnell Douglas Corp MD-11 freighter aircraft and taken options on a further seven.</p>
<p>The Deutsche Lufthansa AG cargo arm said the order, which is subject to final approval by its board, envisages the first five trijets being delivered in 1998, starting in June that year.</p>
<p>Separately McDonnell Douglas said the aircraft will be powered by General Electric engines. It said the order was worth over $550 million for the initial five aircraft and over $1.3 billion if Lufthansa takes all 12 aircraft.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 1 71 542 7717</p>
</text>
